  "title": "Gated Concept Adapters and Intervenable Concept Dynamics",
  "summary": "Gated Concept Adapters (GCA) introduce a layer-wise concept bottleneck framework that enables auditable text understanding, while TRACE-CBM extends this model to forecasting concept dynamics over time. Both GCA and TRACE-CBM provide tools for inspecting, editing, and controlling concept-based predictions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "GCA introduces a layer-wise concept bottleneck framework for auditable text understanding with a compact concept-mediated interface.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "TRACE-CBM extends concept bottleneck models to forecasting by modeling how concept activations evolve over time as activities change.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "GCA and TRACE-CBM both enable inspecting, editing, and controlling concept-based predictions through shared activity classifiers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
